# WINDWARD STAKE — Open Hardware Spec v1.0
### Decorative Vertical-Axis Wind Ornament // Ambient Solar-Hybrid Power // Caged Bird-Safe // Nightlight + Bug Zap
**Status: OPEN SOURCE. Take it, build it, sell it, remix it. No permission required.**
BEKW-CODE public release — EK'VESH'ARUN·7777·KAN

---

## 1. CONCEPT SUMMARY

A yard-stake ornament built around a small vertical-axis wind turbine (VAWT) — not pitched as a primary power source, but as an always-decorative object that happens to ambiently harvest wind, sun, and store both toward useful small loads: a dusk-to-dawn nightlight and a bug zapper. Engineered for total foolproof installation (stake it, done) and zero-rot, zero-bird-harm, zero-maintenance longevity.

**Design ethos:** the "Ferrari meter" reference — every part is *over-engineered for reliability and finish*, not for raw output. The win condition is "beautiful, harmless, never breaks, never needs attention" — power output is a bonus, not the pitch.

---

## 2. MECHANICAL SYSTEM

### 2.1 Turbine
- Vertical-axis wind turbine (Savonius or helical Savonius style — self-starting in any wind direction, no yaw mechanism needed, inherently safer than horizontal-axis for low-altitude ground placement).
- Blade material: UV-stabilized, weather-rated polymer (HDPE or similar) — won't rot, won't rust, won't fatigue-crack from UV like cheap garden-spinner plastics do.
- Sealed magnetic bearing or low-friction ceramic bearing at the rotor axis — spins freely in light breeze (this is the "wind chime" aesthetic requirement: it should move beautifully even when barely generating).

### 2.2 Bird-Safe Cage
- Open-lattice cage surrounding the rotor, gap spacing engineered too narrow for small birds to enter the blade plane, wide enough not to choke airflow meaningfully.
- Cage doubles as the structural mount point for the solar skin and the decorative shape (e.g., the flamingo/ornament silhouette can be built around or onto the cage frame).
- Result: zero blade-strike risk, unlike traditional horizontal turbines — this is a genuine differentiator worth leading with, since bird-strike is the most common objection to wind hardware of any kind.

### 2.3 Stake & Install
- Single ground stake, auger-tip or straight-spike, foolproof one-motion install — no tools required, no electrical wiring on install (fully self-contained unit).
- No moving parts exposed below the cage — stake and lower housing are sealed, static, weatherproof.
- Designed so it is "hard to mess up": no orientation requirement (VAWT doesn't care about wind direction), no calibration, no app pairing, no setup sequence.

---

## 3. POWER SYSTEM

### 3.1 Generation Sources
| Source | Component | Role |
|---|---|---|
| Wind | VAWT rotor + small coreless generator | Ambient primary; opportunistic, not relied upon |
| Solar | Thin-film solar skin wrapped over the decorative shell/cage | Ambient primary; predictable daily contribution |

### 3.2 Storage
- Small sealed LiFePO4 cell (chosen for cycle life and thermal stability outdoors — far more abrasion/heat/cold tolerant than standard LiPo for a unit that lives outside year-round).
- Capacity sized to the actual load (nightlight + zapper), not toward any "off-grid power" claim — this is a low-load buffer, not a battery bank.

### 3.3 Loads
- **Dusk-to-dawn nightlight**: photoresistor-triggered LED, low draw, ambient garden lighting.
- **Bug zapper**: UV-attractant LED + low-current high-voltage grid, active only at dusk/night alongside the light (shared trigger circuit), sized for small-yard insect control, not industrial-scale.
- Simple priority logic: light + zapper draw first from whichever source (solar/wind) is currently generating, battery buffer covers gaps.

### 3.4 Honest Framing
This unit is not a power plant and should never be marketed as one. It is a self-powered ornamental object whose own running costs (light + zapper) are covered by ambient harvest, meaning it requires zero external power, zero batteries-to-replace, and zero electrical hookup — that's the actual value proposition, not "free energy for your house."

