## 4. MATERIALS / BOM (target estimate)

| Part | Material | Est. unit cost @ scale |
|---|---|---|
| VAWT rotor + blades | UV-stable HDPE | $2.20 |
| Coreless micro-generator | Standard low-RPM generator | $1.80 |
| Bird-safe cage | Powder-coated steel or UV-stable polymer lattice | $1.60 |
| Solar skin (thin-film) | Flexible thin-film PV | $2.40 |
| LiFePO4 cell | Small sealed cell | $1.90 |
| LED nightlight module | Photoresistor-triggered LED | $0.50 |
| Bug zapper module | UV LED + low-current HV grid | $1.70 |
| Decorative shell (ornament shape) | Weather-rated polymer or coated metal | $1.50 |
| Stake + housing | Galvanized/coated steel, sealed base | $1.40 |
| **Total est. BOM** | | **~$15.00/unit** |

Target retail: garden-decor tier ($35–55), competitive with decorative solar yard ornaments already on the market, with wind-hybrid + bug zap as the differentiator.

---

## 5. WHY THIS WORKS WHERE OTHER VERTICAL WINDMILLS GET MOCKED

The usual criticism of small vertical garden windmills is fair: as a standalone "power generation" product they're underwhelming, because nobody is pretending the load expectation is small. This spec sidesteps the criticism by never making the power claim the headline:

- It's a decorative kinetic object first (same category as a wind spinner or kinetic yard sculpture) — it has to earn its place in the yard on looks and motion alone.
- The power harvest pays for its own small loads (light, zapper) — a self-sufficiency story, not an output story.
- Bird-safety and zero-rot construction solve the two real objections to outdoor wind hardware (harm and longevity) that horizontal turbines and cheap plastic spinners both fail on.
- "Idiot proof" install (stake, done) removes the friction that kills adoption of anything requiring wiring or calibration.

---

## 6. OPEN SOURCE TERMS

This design is released into the open. No patent claims, no licensing fees, no gatekeeping.
- Build it. Modify it. Manufacture it. Sell it under your own brand.
- Attribution appreciated, not required.
- Third piece in the open hardware set alongside the Chronovolt Case and AdaptaFit shoe — all built on the same inversion principle.

**Inversion principle:** ambient wind and solar harvest, bird-safe turbine geometry, and weatherproof materials all already exist as proven components. Nobody fused them into something that justifies its own yard-space by being beautiful first and useful second.

